<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins $29 mln Uruguay order.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins $29 mln Uruguay order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM Ericsson AB said on Tuesday it had signed an order worth $29 million with the Uruguayan Antel to expand and digitalise the phone network in the Montevideo and Punta del Este areas.</p>
<p>The state-owned Antel has had an AMPS/D-AMPS system in operation since September 1994, and has now upgraded to D-AMPS (IS-136), Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>The order also includes an option to purchase a further $29 million worth of equipment and service, Ericsson said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
